```json

```
EXPERIMENT(Bf)→0 with Bf=(0,1,0) eliminates every hypothesis that evaluates to 1 on that vector, leaving 15 consistent hypotheses: H00, H01, H03, H04, H05, H06, H08, H10, H11, H13, H16, H22, H25, H26, H29.

For the next probe I'll reuse the already-known vector Hs=(1,1,0) (no need to spend a probe). Evaluating the 15 survivors on (1,1,0) splits them 6-vs-9 (predict 1: H00,H05,H13,H16,H25,H26; predict 0: H01,H03,H04,H06,H08,H10,H11,H22,H29), a good discriminating split.

